>I have got one potion of holy water. What (kind of) item is best to be
>blessed (e.g. unicorn horn, luckstone, scroll of identify, scroll of enchant
>something etc.)??

  There is no point blessing weapons. When you wield a weapon while praying
at an altar your god will take care of that for you.

  The first thing I bless is a luckstone. After that a magic marker (if you
have one). I also bless a unicorn horn. I do not know if this is true, but 
it seems that a blessed unicorn horn is more likely to restore lost stats
than an uncursed one. Good scrolls to bless are genocide, charging, enchant
something, and especially remove curse. But if you have only one potion of
holy water, save it to make some more holy water. Dipping unicorn horn into
a potion of blindness, confusion, or sickness will turn it into regular
water. Dipping a bunch of potions of regular water into holy water will
allow you to have many potions of holy water. 

Hope this helps.

